\title{Time to event with competing risks}
\description{
The person-level table the models read, and the two summaries that do not need a model: events and rates per group, and the Aalen-Johansen cumulative incidence.
}
\details{
A person who dies of another cause can no longer reach the outcome. That is not censoring, which means observation stopped: the outcome has become impossible, so the death is treated as a competing event. One minus Kaplan-Meier would overestimate the cumulative incidence, which is why Aalen-Johansen is used.
}
